2. Why is React better than other UI frameworks?

→ React is component-based, so we can reuse UI components and maintain code easily.
→ Its declarative approach makes UI updates easier to manage when application state changes.
→ It has a strong ecosystem, including React Router and state-management libraries.
→ React is not always better; Angular provides more built-in features, while the choice depends on project requirements.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

3. What are the advantages of React Hooks?

→ Hooks allow functional components to manage state and component behaviour.
→ useState manages state, useEffect handles side effects, and useContext shares data.
→ useMemo and useCallback help optimize expensive calculations and function references when needed.
→ Custom hooks allow reusable logic across components.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

4. Explain useMemo with an example.

→ useMemo caches a calculated value between renders until its dependencies change.
→ I use it when a calculation is expensive and its inputs have not changed.

Example:

const filteredStudents = useMemo(() => {
    return students.filter(s => s.marks > 80);
}, [students]);

→ The filtering calculation reruns when the students reference changes.
→ I avoid using useMemo for every calculation because it adds complexity and has its own overhead.

