18. What are idempotent REST API methods?

→ An operation is idempotent when repeating the same request has the same intended effect as making it once.
→ GET: Safe and idempotent.
→ PUT: Idempotent when implemented according to its intended semantics.
→ DELETE: Idempotent in intended effect, although repeated requests may return different status codes.
→ POST is generally not idempotent unless the API explicitly implements idempotency, such as through an idempotency key.

