19. ArrayList vs LinkedList

→ ArrayList uses a dynamic array and provides fast indexed access, typically O(1).
→ LinkedList uses linked nodes and indexed access takes O(n).
→ ArrayList is usually better for reading and iterating through elements.
→ LinkedList can insert or remove elements efficiently when the relevant node position is already available, but locating that position can take O(n).

